      {
        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define safeguarding, confidentiality, and record-keeping standards.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M19",
            "speaker_id": 89329,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, as part of T2, I've drafted the Safeguarding and Confidentiality Procedures (A2). The document is now in the project folder for your review. Please pay close attention to the sections on consent and data handling. All feedback is welcome.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2",
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "page_facing_up",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 61769,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "Thanks, I'm on it. This connects directly to T4 and the data collection templates (A3). A key question for us to decide (D4) is what the absolute minimum data fields are that we need to record for each interaction. Simpler is better for compliance and workload.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T4",
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 1424,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "I'm reading through A2 now. For T8, the record-keeping system, will we need a separate folder for each young person? Or one big file? I'm worried about keeping track of everything.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 89329,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Good question, @1424. The procedures in A2 recommend a secure digital folder for each individual receiving one-to-one support to maintain confidentiality. For general attendance at workshops, a single, anonymised list per session is sufficient. Let's make sure that's clear.",
            "mentions": [
              1424
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 522004,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Regarding D4, I agree with keeping it simple. For evaluation purposes, we need a unique (but anonymised) ID, the date, the type of activity, and the location. This allows us to track engagement patterns without collecting unnecessary personal data.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 98920,
            "reply_to": "M19",
            "text": "In the dental clinic we have very strict rules for patient information. Will these procedures in A2 be enough? I need to be sure before I start.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 89329,
            "reply_to": "M24",
            "text": "A very important point, @98920. This draft is based on social care standards. I've included a note that all health-related information must also adhere to clinical confidentiality guidelines. Before we finalize, I will share A2 with the dental clinic supervisor and the compliance officer for their formal sign-off.",
            "mentions": [
              98920
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 1424,
            "reply_to": "M22",
            "text": "Ok, that makes sense. So for T8 I will plan for individual folders for the one-to-one support cases.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 61769,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "So for the minimum data fields (D4), are we agreeing on: Anonymised ID, Date, Activity Type, Location? I can build the template in A3 around that right away.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 89329,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "Yes, let's confirm that. Decision D4: The minimum data fields for all interactions will be Anonymised ID, Date, Activity Type, and Location. Any objections?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 522004,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "None from me. That's a solid foundation.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 1424,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Agreed.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 61769,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Great, I'll proceed with the templates (A3) based on this.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M32",
            "speaker_id": 89329,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "Perfect. I'll incorporate the feedback into A2 and send it for final review. Assuming no major issues are raised by the external stakeholders, we can consider the procedures approved by tomorrow EOD. That will close out decision D3.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
